abstract: "A physics-informed post-hoc reliability framework for Zero-Noise Extrapolation
  in NISQ circuits. Introduces (i) a fluid-dynamic stability filter based on a discrete
  H1 Sobolev regularity functional on the ZNE curve, and (ii) five structured noise
  scaling schedules (Fibonacci, Lucas, prime-anchored, linear, odd-integer) evaluated
  against all four standard extrapolants (linear, Richardson, poly-2, poly-3).
  Validated across 153,600 simulation runs (4 circuit types x 5 schedules x 4
  extrapolants x 3 qubit counts x 8 depths x 8 noise levels x 10 trials) and 120
  hardware trials on IBM Quantum processors ibm_fez (Heron r2) and ibm_torino
  (Heron r1). All 24 hardware conditions pass the simulation-calibrated threshold
  Gamma=0.05 with maximum observed epsilon=0.00285 (5.7% of Gamma)."
